  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Interruptions to maritime routes increase diversion and inspection risk for dual‑use and sensitive cargoes, prompting US regulators to broaden licensing requirements and tighten export controls on shipments transiting high‑risk corridors (including tighter scrutiny of goods destined for China).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_iran_standoff</data>
