<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diplomatic_tension" target="ai_infrastructure_risk::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising interstate diplomatic friction around control/use of communications and services triggers governments to open export controls, investment reviews, sanctions and other regulatory actions specifically targeting AI infrastructure and service relationships, raising overall scrutiny.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_infrastructure_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diplomatic_tension" target="euro_bond_fragment::sovereign_risk_premium" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising diplomatic tension (threats of sanctions, export controls, or reciprocal measures) raises the perceived probability of cross‑border economic disruption for specific European sovereigns, so investors demand wider country‑specific spreads.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">euro_bond_fragment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diplomatic_tension" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::inst_coop_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating diplomatic friction tied to the conflict leads governments to suspend or downgrade formal regulatory dialogues, joint standard-setting bodies, and information-sharing arrangements, directly reducing institutional cooperation between major powers.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::diplomatic_tension" target="us_iran_standoff::military_proxy_violence" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising diplomatic tension between Russia and Western states over the Ukraine war prompts Russia to deepen military-technical cooperation with Iran (e.g., transfers, training), which raises proxy groups' strike capability and leads to more intense attacks against US-aligned targets.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
