<edge source="ai_infrastructure_risk::special_cloud_stability" target="euro_bond_fragment::bond_market_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A decline in the financial stability of specialized cloud providers (or their insolvency) creates immediate counterparty risk, margin calls and forced asset sales that spike sovereign bond volatility; conversely greater stability dampens volatility.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_infrastructure_risk</data>
  <data key="d39">euro_bond_fragment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_infrastructure_risk::special_cloud_stability" target="russia_ukraine_war::political_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">When specialized cloud providers are more financially stable, governments and militaries have less need and leverage to intervene or press providers to re-prioritize or commandeer services, reducing the frequency and intensity of political requests to operators.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_infrastructure_risk</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_infrastructure_risk::special_cloud_stability" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::inst_coop_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Financial stress or failures among specialized cloud providers with cross‑border footprints incentivize governments to negotiate joint contingency protocols, data access arrangements, or supervisory coordination to limit systemic disruption.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_infrastructure_risk</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_infrastructure_risk::special_cloud_stability" target="us_iran_standoff::energy_trade_flow_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved financial stability of specialized cloud providers preserves the digital backbone for chartering, port clearances and hazardous-cargo approvals, allowing higher throughput of oil and gas shipments; instability reduces that throughput when operators restrict operations preemptively.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_infrastructure_risk</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
