<edge source="euro_bond_fragment::sovereign_borrowing_cost" target="ai_infrastructure_risk::special_cloud_stability" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher sovereign borrowing costs lift baseline interest rates and corporate refinancing spreads, increasing debt-servicing and refinancing pressures on specialized cloud and AI infrastructure firms and thereby eroding their solvency margins.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">euro_bond_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_infrastructure_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="euro_bond_fragment::sovereign_borrowing_cost" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::tech_transfer_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher sovereign borrowing costs in the euro area raise financing costs for firms and reduce available public support for international R&amp;D and joint ventures, causing a measurable decline in the pace of technology transfers between European firms and Chinese partners.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">euro_bond_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
