<edge source="euro_bond_fragment::safe_haven_capital_flow" target="ai_infrastructure_risk::infra_deploy_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Large shifts of institutional capital into safe‑haven assets reduce available project and venture financing for higher‑risk infrastructure, causing postponement or cancellation of AI data‑center, chip fab, and specialized hosting deployments.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">euro_bond_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_infrastructure_risk</data>
</edge>
<edge source="euro_bond_fragment::safe_haven_capital_flow" target="us_iran_standoff::energy_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in capital flows from Europe into dollar-denominated safe havens (USD/US Treasuries) typically strengthens the dollar, which mechanically depresses dollar-priced crude and gas prices, reducing the aggregated energy-price level.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">euro_bond_fragment</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_standoff</data>
</edge>
